    "q-7621": {
      "dom_id": "step-q7621",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the remainder when $q(x)=5x-{x}^{2}$ is divided by $x-4.$",
      "worked_solution": "The remainder theorem states that when $q(x)$ is divided by $(x-4),$ the remainder equals $q(4).$ \n\nEvaluating $q(4)$ directly gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q(4) & =5(4)-(4)^{2} \\\\  & =20-16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, when $q(x)$ is divided by $(x-4),$ the remainder is $4.$\n\n**Note:** We can check the answer by carrying out synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-1$ | $5$ | $0$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-4$ | $4$ |\n|  | $-1$ | $1$ | $4$ |",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
